  <title>Algemene update week 12</title>
  <link>https://www.ect.nl/nl/nieuws/dossiers/n4-euromax/algemene-update-week-12</link>
  <description>  &lt;div class="layout layout--onecol"&gt;
    &lt;div class="layout__region layout__region--content"&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="field field--name-node-post-date field--type-ds field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;19 March 2026 - 16:08&lt;/div&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;&lt;p&gt;Two months ago, we started the migration to the new Terminal Operating System (TOS) at the ECT Euromax terminal. Over the past period, numerous adjustments have been made to the systems to improve stability. We are steadily seeing improvements in the operation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deepsea and Feeder&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;For the handling of deepsea and feeder vessels, there has been continuous close coordination with the involved shipping lines. In addition to the TOS implementation, extreme weather conditions have also had a very negative impact on overall operations. Productivity is gradually increasing, which is also improving handling capacity. The final steps still need to be taken to fully return to previous performance levels.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rail, Barge and Truck&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;In recent weeks, we have kept you informed via Service Messages about the situation and the disruptions occurring on the landside of the ECT Euromax terminal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately, we have had to activate the D-route for &lt;strong&gt;road transport&lt;/strong&gt; on a regular basis due to various disruptions in the gate and/or terminal processes. This has resulted in long waiting times and occasional lack of clarity for road transport. We sincerely apologize for this. Through our Service Messages, we will provide more specific information in the event of new disruptions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Productivity for &lt;strong&gt;barges&lt;/strong&gt; is in line with expectations. Through the Nextlogic planning tool, barges are still being scheduled with an adjusted number of moves per hour. Productivity is gradually increasing, which is also improving handling capacity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;is running stably with adjusted productivity levels. The rail schedule has been aligned accordingly in close cooperation with operators and carriers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finally&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We would like to thank you for your involvement, patience, and flexibility during the migration to the new TOS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With this update, we conclude the series of migration updates. From this point onward, no separate updates will be sent. Further information and relevant announcements will, where necessary, be shared via our Weekly Update, for which you can subscribe via &lt;a href="mailto:customer_info@ect.nl"&gt;customer_info@ect.nl&lt;/a&gt;, and via our Service Messages. These Service Messages can be received through the ECT App and reviewed on &lt;a href="http://www.ect.nl" target="_new"&gt;www.ect.nl&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Should you have any questions following this update, please do not hesitate to contact us. Inland shipping operators can, as usual, contact CAL, and feeder operators can contact CAF. For rail transport, rail operators and carriers can direct their questions to CAR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For all other inquiries, please contact the Customer Service Desk at +31 (0)181 278088 or via &lt;a href="mailto:customerservice@ect.nl"&gt;customerservice@ect.nl&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are confident in the continued progress of the migration. All information can be found in the TOS Euromax dossier via: &lt;a href="https://www.ect.nl/nl/tos-euromax" target="_new"&gt;https://www.ect.nl/nl/tos-euromax&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

</description>
