<item>
  <title>General update week 8</title>
  <link>https://www.ect.nl/en/news/dossiers/n4-euromax/general-update-week-8</link>
  <description>  &lt;div class="layout layout--onecol"&gt;
    &lt;div class="layout__region layout__region--content"&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="field field--name-node-post-date field--type-ds field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;17 February 2026 - 19:16&lt;/div&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;&lt;p&gt;We are now four weeks into the migration to the new Terminal Operating System (TOS) at the ECT Euromax terminal. We are steadily seeing progress in operations, but unfortunately, we are still dealing with several challenges.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Deepsea and Feeder&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For the handling of deepsea vessels, continuous close consultation is taking place with the involved shippinglines. In the meantime, discharge and loading operations have been carried out on both one and two deepsea vessels simultaneously.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Production levels in the handling of these vessels show a mixed picture. Some of the waterside disruptions experienced in recent weeks have now been resolved, while others have been assigned to our suppliers. Compared to earlier communications, current production levels are still below the desired estimates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rail, Barge and Truck&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In recent weeks, we have informed you via Service Messages about the situation and occurring disruptions on the landside of the ECT Euromax terminal.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Unfortunately, we have had to activate the D-route for road transport several times due to various disruptions in the gate process. This has resulted in long waiting times and, at times, uncertainty for road carriers. Our apologies for this. Through our Service Messages, we will try to provide more specific information in the event of new disruptions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Production levels for inland shipping are in line with expectations. Through Nextlogic’s planning tool, we are still scheduling barges with an adjusted number of moves per hour. Unfortunately, inland shipping has also been affected by the aforementioned waterside disruptions. We expect to see improvements in barge productivity in the coming period.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For rail operations, the number of trains handled daily is increasing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finally&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We would like to thank you for your involvement, patience, and flexibility during the migration to the new TOS.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have any questions following this update, please let us know. Inland shipping operators should contact CAL as usual. For rail transport, rail operators and carriers can contact CAR with their questions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For other inquiries, you can reach the Customer Service Desk at&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;+31(0)181 278088 or &lt;a href="mailto:customerservice@ect.nl"&gt;customerservice@ect.nl&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are confident about the further progress of the migration. All information can be found in our TOS Euromax dossier, available at:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://www.ect.nl/en/tos-euromax"&gt;https://www.ect.nl/en/tos-euromax&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
      
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;

</description>
