<item>
  <title>Markt update 30-1-2026</title>
  <link>https://www.ect.nl/nl/nieuws/dossiers/n4-euromax/markt-update-30-1-2026</link>
  <description>  &lt;div class="layout layout--onecol"&gt;
    &lt;div class="layout__region layout__region--content"&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="field field--name-node-post-date field--type-ds field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;30 January 2026 - 14:40&lt;/div&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;&lt;p&gt;We have now been migrating to the new Terminal Operating System (TOS) at the ECT Euromax terminal for almost two weeks, and we are seeing stable progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are confident that the Go-live will continue to proceed, but we will continue to monitor the operation closely. Further information about the migration will be provided through the various communication channels from now on. However, all current information can still be found on our website; our TOS Euromax dossier can be accessed at:&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="https://www.ect.nl/nl/tos-euromax"&gt;https://www.ect.nl/nl/tos-euromax&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For deepsea vessels, the planning is carried out in close consultation with the shipping companies involved. Feeders are scheduled as usual via CAF and barges via CAL.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Communication for road transport is via service messages. For rail transport, the planning is via CAR.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For questions, you can also contact the Customer Service Desk at +31 (0)181 278088 or&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href="mailto:customerservice@ect.nl"&gt;customerservice@ect.nl&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
