<item>
  <title>Algemene update week 4</title>
  <link>https://www.ect.nl/nl/nieuws/dossiers/n4-euromax/algemene-update-week-4</link>
  <description>  &lt;div class="layout layout--onecol"&gt;
    &lt;div class="layout__region layout__region--content"&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="field field--name-node-post-date field--type-ds field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;23 January 2026 - 15:41&lt;/div&gt;
      
            &lt;div class="clearfix text-formatted field field--name-body field--type-text-with-summary field--label-hidden field__item"&gt;&lt;p&gt;Dear relation,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have now been working on the migration to the new Terminal Operating System (TOS) at the ECT Euromax terminal for almost a week. More detailed information about the progress of this process is provided below.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On Tuesday, January 20th, the operational processes were restarted in phases. As expected, this has resulted in some disruptions. The support teams on hand have been able to resolve these quickly so far. So far, we are satisfied with the progress of the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;On the waterside, deepsea, feeder, and barge operations have already commenced. The first deepsea vessel, the Cosco Shipping Andes, has left the terminal ahead of schedule. The next vessel is arriving. Further planning is taking place in close consultation with the shipping companies involved. Two combined berths are currently being used for handling feeders and barges. Scheduling for feeders is handled as usual via CAF and for barges via CAL.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the landside, the process is also being scaled up gradually. Separate communication regarding truck handling is being provided via service messages. Truck handling is also progressing better than originally expected. Therefore, it will be further expanded. Based on the current situation, it has been decided to discontinue the D-route with immediate effect. Direct visits to the ECT Euromax terminal are now possible again. Rail handling is currently still limited, with scheduling handled by CAR.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We will continue to keep you informed throughout the migration through various communication channels. All current information will be published on our website. A dedicated file has been opened for this purpose and can be accessed at: &lt;a href="https://www.ect.nl/nl/tos-euromax"&gt;https://www.ect.nl/nl/tos-euromax&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For questions, you can also contact the Customer Service Desk at +31(0)181 278088 or &lt;a href="mailto:customerservice@ect.nl"&gt;customerservice@ect.nl&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ECT is not responsible for the timely delivery of this message.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
